cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use swelter, please cite it using this metadata. Cite published data separately using the snapshot's DATA-CITATION.cff."
title: "swelter"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, community-operated heat and air-quality sensing pipeline with
  an accessible public map and data explorer. swelter validates and quarantines
  node payloads, keeps raw measurements immutable, applies versioned calibration
  corrections, and publishes QC, uncertainty, source, freshness, time-window,
  and calibration provenance through a bilingual interface. Current reading and
  Readings link history, distribution, evidence, map, table, list, and export
  views. The software is Apache-2.0; environmental data retains source-specific
  terms, with CC0 used only for project-authored synthetic data or authorized
  first-party observations.
type: software
authors:
